course: dictionary
lesson: 15772
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context, the words around them, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «The workers cut a block of tuff from the old cliff.» Here tuff is a light, rough rock made from volcanic ash that has been pressed and stuck together over time.
explain: «That skateboard trick was tuff!» Here tuff is slang. It is a playful spelling of tough, and it means cool or impressive. The rock meaning would make no sense in this sentence.
explain: Ask yourself: what do the other words point to? Cliff and block point to rock. Trick and skateboard point to slang. When you find your meaning, swap it into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Tuff is a noun for a light, rough rock made from volcanic ash.
fact: Tuff is an uncountable noun, so we say some tuff, not two tuffs.
fact: Slang «tuff» is a playful spelling of «tough», and it means cool, impressive or hard.
fact: Tuff tells a reader that a volcano once erupted nearby.
fact: Ancient Romans and the people of Easter Island carved and built with tuff because it is soft enough to cut.
exercise: «The wall was made of pale, light tuff rock.» What is tuff in this sentence? | A sweet bread | A fast car | *A light, rough rock made from volcanic ash | A soft cloud in the sky
exercise: Jamie says, «That goal was tuff!» What does tuff mean? | Very cold | *Cool and impressive | Made from volcanic ash | Very quiet
exercise: «Long ago, a volcano threw out ash that became tuff.» Which word is a clue that tuff is a rock? | long | *volcano | became | threw
test: «Mia found a piece of tuff on the volcano trip.» What is tuff in this sentence? | *A light, rough rock | A type of cat | A cool dance move | A loud shout
test: Ben wrote, «Your new bike is tuff, bro.» What does tuff mean here? | *Cool and impressive | Old and broken | A rock from a volcano | Wet and grey
exam: Which meaning fits best in «Our class tested the tuff from the cliff»? | Cool and impressive | A kind of bike | *A light, rough rock | A loud noise
